{"name":"Half Pearl Lusta","hex":"#f1ead7","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"half","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of two usually roughly equal parts into which anything may be divided, or considered as divided.","One of two equal periods into which a game is divided."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Consisting of a half (½, 50%).","Consisting of some indefinite portion resembling a half; approximately a half, whether more or less; partial; imperfect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/half"},{"term":"pearl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shelly concretion, usually rounded, and having a brilliant luster, with varying tints, found in the mantle, or between the mantle and shell, of certain bivalve mollusks, especially in the pearl oysters and river mussels, and sometimes in certain univalves. It is usually due to a secretion of shelly substance around some irritating foreign particle. Its substance is the same as nacre, or mother-of-pearl. Round lustrous pearls are used in jewellery.","Something precious."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To set or adorn with pearls, or with mother-of-pearl.","To cause to resemble pearls in shape; to make into small round grains."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pearl"}],"entries":[{"title":"One half","blocks":[{"text":"One half is the multiplicative inverse of 2. It is an irreducible fraction with a numerator of 1 and a denominator of 2. It often appears in mathematical equations, recipes and measurements."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_half"},{"title":"Pearl","blocks":[{"text":"A pearl is a hard, shiny object produced within the soft tissue of a living shelled mollusk. Like the shell of a mollusk, a pearl is composed of calcium carbonate in a crystalline form, which is deposited in concentric layers. More commercially valuable pearls are perfectly round and smooth, but many other shapes, known as baroque pearls, can occur. The highest quality of natural pearls have been highly valued as gemstones and objects of beauty for many centuries. In literature, pearls have become a metaphor for something rare, fine, admirable, and valuable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Various_pearls.jpg/330px-Various_pearls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearl"},{"title":"Pearl (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color pearl is a pale tint of off-white. It is a representation of the average color of a pearl."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/PerlmuttAusst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearl_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Eye_of_Horus_square.png/330px-Eye_of_Horus_square.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Eye_of_Horus_square.png/330px-Eye_of_Horus_square.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A square of side length one, here dissected into rectangles whose areas are successive powers of one half","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEye_of_Horus_square.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Ireland-Stamp-1940-HalfCentPostageDue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Ireland-Stamp-1940-HalfCentPostageDue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Postal stamp, Ireland, 1940: one halfpenny postage due","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIreland-Stamp-1940-HalfCentPostageDue.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Various_pearls.jpg/500px-Variou